~ start
# Everything a conversation can do with the people standing in it.
#
# Point a DialogueInteractable at this title to watch it, or copy the lines you
# want into your own scripts. Names are combatant keys ("cyrus", "alithia") or
# the name of a node placed on the map. Places are either a Waypoint's name or
# a tile - walk("cyrus", "gate") and walk("cyrus", 12, 7) both work.

cyrus: Someone's coming up the road.

# Walks in from off the map. The line after it waits until they arrive.
do Actors.enter("barbarian", 14, 13)
barbarian: Far enough. This road's closed.

# Walking to meet them, then turning to look at each other.
do Actors.walk("cyrus", 13, 13)
do Actors.face("barbarian", "cyrus")
do Actors.face("cyrus", "barbarian")
cyrus: Closed by whom?

# _behind starts the walk and lets the talking carry on over it, so someone can
# cross the scene while a conversation continues.
do Actors.walk_behind("alithia", 13, 15)
barbarian: By me. Turn around.
alithia: He's alone, Cyrus.

# Waiting for a walk started earlier, when the next line needs them there.
do Actors.finished("alithia")
alithia: And he's bluffing.

# Walks off the map. Anyone the conversation invented is gone with it; a party
# member is only walked out of sight, since they are still the player's.
do Actors.exit("barbarian")
cyrus: ...he was, at that.

=> END
